# Review: DebugPlugin

The debug panel is solid and well covered: the hidden `root/debug` category has a unit test, and the
panel's stories play the drawer toggle, the dock/float switch, the console-first default and the restored
view state. The other features (Generate objects, the object Debug companion, the space-objects companion,
the wireframe overlay and the stats cards) are all contributed as the spec describes but have no test or
story that drives them. The QA section is the weak spot for automation: QA-1 and QA-2 have nothing, QA-3
has only the template's seed test, and QA-4 to QA-9 are walked by autocue demo flows that record the steps
rather than assert their `expect` lines. No divergences found. The spec declares both a `component` and a `feat` named `DebugPanel`; one verdict covers both, since
the checker keys verdicts by id. Of 21 items (20 distinct ids): 5 done, 7 untested, 7 partial, 0 diverged,
2 missing, counting the shared verdict once per item.

## Extensions

